From bdd1276f3958b17dd40c036e60d476383c7e08b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MicroNUX contributors <micronux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 05:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 15/46] mmc: dw: reprogram clock only on slot change

Dual-slot arbitration forced a full clock reinitialization before every
request.  The ESP32-P4 sequence disables the card clock and sends three
update-clock commands, so a 4 KiB block workload repeated that sequence tens
of thousands of times even while consecutive requests remained on the same
slot.  Under concurrent SD and SDIO traffic the controller eventually wedged
inside a later slot-0 request.

Remember whether arbitration actually selected a different slot.  Continue
calling the common setup helper for every request so it can maintain the bus
width, but force the clock command sequence only when the physical slot
changes.  A frequency change on the same slot is still handled by the
helper's normal clock comparison.

Signed-off-by: MicroNUX contributors <micronux@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
@@ -1460,6 +1460,7 @@ static void __dw_mci_start_request(struct dw_mci *host,
 	struct mmc_request *mrq;
 	struct mmc_data	*data;
 	u32 cmdflags;
+	bool slot_changed;
 
 	if (host->multi_slot) {
 		host->request_seq++;
@@ -1467,8 +1468,9 @@ static void __dw_mci_start_request(struct dw_mci *host,
 		host->request_started = jiffies;
 	}
+	slot_changed = host->slot != slot;
 	host->slot = slot;
 	if (host->multi_slot)
-		dw_mci_setup_bus(slot, true);
+		dw_mci_setup_bus(slot, slot_changed);
 
 	mrq = slot->mrq;
 
